ReScript File
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// Unbraced attribute values across the whole class ReScript allows.')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// An unbraced value is a *primary* expression — an atomic expression followed by')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// call, index and field postfixes. The compiler says so directly: its JSX parser')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// parses prop values with `parse_primary_expr ~operand:(parse_atomic_expr p)`.')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// `(` and `[` open a region whose interior lexes as ordinary expression text,')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// which is why `b=Some(-1)` works while `b=-1` still cannot form — `-` is')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// unlexable in a tag, and that guards where a value STARTS (see')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// JsxInvalidNegativeAttributeValue, the sentinel for not overreaching here).')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// Two lines diverge from bsc deliberately, in opposite directions: `listValue`')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// (bsc accepts, the grammar cannot spell it) and `uppercaseField` (bsc rejects,')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// the grammar takes it anyway). Every other line below is accepted by both.')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// Constructor application — the shape reported from production')
